---
// What dependency_overrides[get_current_user] removes. Numbers: test_api_auth.py,
// POST /purge as bob (read-only scope): 403 with a real token, 200 with the override.
const W = 900, H = 330;
const steps = [
  { en: 'read the token', vi: 'đọc token' },
  { en: 'verify signature + expiry', vi: 'kiểm chữ ký + hạn' },
  { en: 'check the scopes', vi: 'kiểm scope' },
];
---
<figure class="bep9d">
  <div class="bep9d-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Top: get_current_user is three steps, read the token, verify signature and expiry, check the scopes; a real token for bob on POST /purge ends in 403. Bottom: dependency_overrides replaces the whole function with a lambda returning bob, so the three steps are skipped and the same request returns 200.">
    <text x="20" y="28" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>real token</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>token thật</tspan>
    </text>
    {steps.map((s, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={20 + i * 215} y="44" width="190" height="56" rx="10" class="box" />
        <text x={115 + i * 215} y="77" text-anchor="middle" class="st">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{s.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{s.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
        {i < 2 && <g>
          <line x1={210 + i * 215} y1="72" x2={225 + i * 215} y2="72" class="ln" />
          <polygon points={`${235 + i * 215},72 ${225 + i * 215},67 ${225 + i * 215},77`} class="hd" />
        </g>}
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1="660" y1="72" x2="680" y2="72" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="690,72 680,67 680,77" class="hd" />
    <text x="702" y="68" class="big"><tspan data-lang-en>403</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>403</tspan></text>
    <text x="702" y="88" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>missing scope</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>thiếu scope</tspan></text>

    <line x1="20" y1="140" x2="880" y2="140" class="sep" />

    <text x="20" y="176" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>with the override</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>khi có override</tspan>
    </text>
    {steps.map((s, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={20 + i * 215} y="192" width="190" height="56" rx="10" class="box ghost" />
        <text x={115 + i * 215} y="225" text-anchor="middle" class="st ghostt">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{s.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{s.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1="20" y1="270" x2="640" y2="270" class="strike" />
    <text x="20" y="300" class="code">lambda: "bob"</text>
    <text x="160" y="300" class="bs"><tspan data-lang-en>replaces all three steps</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>thay cả ba bước</tspan></text>
    <line x1="660" y1="220" x2="680" y2="220" class="ln" />
    <polygon points="690,220 680,215 680,225" class="hd" />
    <text x="702" y="216" class="big red"><tspan data-lang-en>200</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>200</tspan></text>
    <text x="702" y="236" class="bs red"><tspan data-lang-en>same request, no check</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>cùng request, không kiểm</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>An override is convenient because it deletes the whole guard, and that is also its trap. The test that needs the guard has to build a real token.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Override tiện vì nó xóa sạch lớp bảo vệ, và đó cũng chính là cái bẫy. Test nào cần đến lớp bảo vệ thì phải tự dựng token thật.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep9d { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep9d-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep9d svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; }
  .bep9d text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep9d .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep9d .st { font-size: 13.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9d .ghostt { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .bep9d .big { font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9d .big.red, .bep9d .bs.red { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep9d .bs { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep9d .code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9d .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep9d .ghost { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; fill: none; }
  .bep9d .ln { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bep9d .hd { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .bep9d .sep { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .bep9d .strike { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 2.2; }
  .bep9d figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
